entry.summary:
This walks through the exact config, the two values you type twice, and the tool-scoping glob that keeps 16 health tools out of your coding context until you actually ask for them.
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "mcp": {
    "health-export": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["npx", "-y", "health-export-mcp"],
      "enabled": true,
      "environment": {
        "HEALTH_DATA_DIR": "/Users/you/Library/Mobile Documents/iCloud~ai~healthexport~app/Documents"
      }
    }
  }
}

type and command are required for a local server, and command is an array, not a shell string, so you cannot chain with &&. HEALTH_DATA_DIR points at the folder holding your .health-cache.json. The server reads that local file and makes zero runtime network calls, so nothing leaves the mac…
